`/data/ylwang/non-textfuzz/target/_audit_result/FFmpeg/report-drafts/libavcodec_jpeg2000dec_c__001.md` has been written with the full report. The vulnerability is a confirmed OOB heap read in `get_cap()` (`libavcodec/jpeg2000dec.c:462–464`): a CAP marker with `len=8` and `Pcap=0xFFFFFFFF` causes 31 excess `bytestream2_get_be16u` calls, reading 62 bytes past the segment boundary. The 62-byte over-read lands within FFmpeg's 64-byte allocation padding and avoids a hard ASAN crash in the standard code path, but would be a `heap-buffer-overflow` in any caller without that padding.
